{"term":"anticipate","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:1ac14a46621e647401","definition":"To act before (someone), especially to prevent an action.","example":"c. 1824 (written, published in 1891) Robert Hall, Fragment on Popery\nWhen two parties, each formidable for their numbers, and the weight of their influence and property, are animated by an equal degree of zeal, it is natural to anticipate the final success of that which possesses the most inherent strength.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["preclude","provide","preempt","discount"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["anticipable","anticipatable","anticipately","anticipatingly","anticipative","anticipator","unanticipating"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/anticipate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c4f4029d9e9a501518","definition":"To take up or introduce (something) prematurely.","example":"The advocate plans to anticipate a part of her argument.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["anticipable","anticipatable","anticipately","anticipatingly","anticipative","anticipator","unanticipating"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/anticipate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:115208dd6c8c781e1a","definition":"To know of (something) before it happens; to expect.","example":"to anticipate the pleasures of a visit","pos":"verb","synonyms":["expect","foretaste","foresee"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["anticipable","anticipatable","anticipately","anticipatingly","anticipative","anticipator","unanticipating"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/anticipate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ad4472d48281ca8425","definition":"To eagerly wait for (something)","example":"Little Johnny started to anticipate the arrival of Santa Claus a week before Christmas.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["look forward to"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["anticipable","anticipatable","anticipately","anticipatingly","anticipative","anticipator","unanticipating"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/anticipate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/ænˈtɪs.ɪ.peɪt/"},"wordFamily":["anticipable","anticipatable","anticipately","anticipatingly","anticipative","anticipator","unanticipating"]}